.TH MANAGEDISKS 1 "2026-10-09" "ManageDisks 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
managedisks \- graphical disk and partition manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B managedisks
[\fB\-\-unlock\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\fR] [\fB\-\-scheme\fR \fIsystem\fR|\fIlight\fR|\fIdark\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B managedisks
shows every disk with a proportional map of its partitions and lets you
create, delete, format, resize, move, copy and check partitions, change
labels, types and flags, convert between MBR and GPT, wipe disks, inspect
drive health (S.M.A.R.T.), run surface tests, clone disks and write or create
disk images.
.PP
Changes are queued as pending operations and previewed before anything is
written. Nothing touches a disk until you press \fBApply\fR.
.PP
The window runs as your normal user. Administrator rights are requested
through polkit (pkexec) only when needed: when you press \fBUnlock\fR or
apply changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-unlock
Ask for administrator rights immediately at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-loop
Show loop devices (disk images attached with losetup).
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme " mode"
Override the color scheme. The default follows the desktop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ManageDisks/ManageDisks.conf
Window layout and preferences.
.TP
.I /var/log/managedisks/operations.log
Record of every operation that was applied.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR managedisks-cli (1),
.BR sfdisk (8),
.BR mkfs (8),
.BR cryptsetup (8),
.BR smartctl (8)
